{
  "decline_reason": "",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The precise requirements depend on which deadline you seek to extend; your question does not identify that deadline.",
      "quotes": [],
      "authority": "none"
    },
    {
      "text": "For the opposition extensions described in Part 49, you must establish both the grounds for the extension and sufficient reason why the extension request itself was not filed in time.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part49/2/2/3/3",
          "quote": "In granting an extension of time, the Registrar must be satisfied as to the grounds set out in the application and the reasons given in support of those grounds. If the extension application was filed out of time, the Registrar must also be satisfied that there was sufficient reason for the application not being made within time (regs 9.12, 17A.48M)."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "For those opposition extensions, establishing the extension ground alone does not ensure that a late request will be granted.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part49/2/2/3/3",
          "quote": "If the extension application was made out of time, that is, after the period for filing the notice of intention to oppose or statement of grounds and particulars had ended, the Registrar will not necessarily grant the extension even if the extension ground has been made out (regs 9.12(2), 17A.48M(2))."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under the Manual’s general extension procedure, the supporting declaration should set out the facts supporting the extension grounds and explain why the request is late.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part15/5/5/2",
          "quote": "The declaration should support the grounds for the application by setting out the facts on which the grounds for requiring the extension are based. If the application is made after the period has expired, the declaration should also set out why the application is late."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "Where section 224(2) applies, the Registrar may grant an extension on a compliant application if an error or omission by the person or their agent, or circumstances beyond the person’s control, caused the relevant act not to be done within time or prevented it being done within time.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMA1995/s224",
          "quote": "(2) If, because of: (a) an error or omission by the person concerned or by his or her agent; or (b) circumstances beyond the control of the person concerned; a relevant act that is required by this Act to be done within a certain time is not, or cannot be, done within that time, the Registrar may, on application made by the person concerned in accordance with the regulations, extend the time for doing the act."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "legislation"
    },
    {
      "text": "Section 224(3) also permits an extension on a compliant application where the relevant act is not, or cannot be, done within time and the Registrar considers that special circumstances justify an extension.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMA1995/s224",
          "quote": "(3) If: (a) a relevant act that a person is required by this Act to do within a certain time is not, or cannot be, done within that time; and (b) on application made by that person in accordance with the regulations, the Registrar is of the opinion that special circumstances exist that justify an extension of that time; the Registrar may extend the time for doing the act."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "legislation"
    },
    {
      "text": "If the request concerns time for acceptance, the Manual requires a late request to include the appropriate fee and a declaration addressing both the need for the extension and the reasons for filing the request late—even within the six-month ‘easy’ extension period.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part16/1/1/4",
          "quote": "Therefore, if an application for an extension of time is made after the time has expired, even if it is within its six month \"easy\" extension period, it will still have to be made under the provisions of section 224(4) and regulation 21.25."
        },
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part16/1/1/4",
          "quote": "These provide that a late application for an extension of time must be accompanied by a declaration setting out both the grounds for needing an extension of time, and also the reasons the application for the extension was not filed in time (together with the appropriate fee)."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    }
  ],
  "declined": false,
  "concepts_used": [
    "GC-0097",
    "GC-0040",
    "GC-0093"
  ]
}
